# Line endings
#
# Every text file in this project is stored and served with LF. The app is a
# static site: the bytes in the repo are the bytes the host sends to the tablet,
# so keeping LF in the repo keeps production identical to the working copy.
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true (system gitconfig). Without
# these rules that setting rewrites every checked-out file to CRLF, which makes
# GitHub Desktop warn about each one and turns a one-line edit into a
# whole-file diff on the next clone. The rules below override autocrlf.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files must stay CRLF. cmd.exe can mis-parse LF-only files that
# contain labels or multi-line blocks.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never normalise these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
